Release notes for pqfreebsd_kernel (pqk).

This file describes new user-visible features, changes and updates relevant to
users of binary or out-of-tree builds of this deliverable.  Each entry should
describe the change in no more than several sentences and should reference
manual pages or sysctl(8) names where an interested user can find more
information.  Entries should wrap after 80 columns.  Each entry should begin
with one or more commit IDs on one line, specified as a comma separated list
and/or range, followed by a colon and a newline.  Entries should be separated
by a newline.

PQFreeBSD is the official non-fancy project name.  Free(ly)B(le)S(se)D (Freely
Blessed) is the evocative Unix-style expansion that still reads FreeBSD.  pqk
is short for Public Quantum Free Berkeley Software Distribution Kernel.
Module .ko basenames remain pqfreebsd and pqfreebsd_*.

This deliverable is not LLM-dependent.  pqf skills consume installed modules;
they do not build this tree on demand.

76b3fa1f9903,7d1281bd791d,d7252b8042a2,779065383714:
	Introduce pqfreebsd(4)-style out-of-tree KLDs.  pqfreebsd.ko is the
	skeletal core (always required).  pqfreebsd_compat_zfs_multilabel.ko
	is a ZFS-only accommodation: OpenZFS mounts that omit MNT_MULTILABEL
	(UFS/FFS already set it) get the flag when effective xattr is on/dir
	or sa (local or inherited).  A proper ZFS multilabel fix will go
	upstream.  See mount(8), zfs(8), and mac(4).

c841acb1057f,056a19b7dcae,aa3a93053f63:
	pqfreebsd.ko maintains suite enforcement and audit state via
	security.pqfreebsd.enforcement and security.pqfreebsd.audit (default
	off, CTLFLAG_RWTUN).  Changes are logged with log(9).  The core does
	not kldload sibling modules; userland / loader does.  The core is the
	clean path to lock down kernels without modifying FreeBSD source.

c5707a00c99d,4ba61178b08d:
	Module hygiene aligned with shipped FreeBSD KLD practice: plain ints
	for state (cf. mac_seeotheruids(4)), MOD_QUIESCE before eventhandler
	teardown (cf. siftr(4)), mountlist + vfs_busy locking (cf. g_journal),
	and log(9) instead of printf for messages.

e217e27ac2ec,41664feb1dcd:
	Steady-state load is ideally loader(8) preload via loader.conf(5)
	(pqfreebsd_load="YES"; ZFS hosts also
	pqfreebsd_compat_zfs_multilabel_load="YES").  kldload(8) is only a
	same-session fallback until reboot.  Later ideal: full TPM e2e on
	that loader path (not this cut).

c7b313101c0c:
	Document mid-install continuity: the try-out host is half-installed
	with pqf skills, paused on the ZFS MNT_MULTILABEL blocker.  After
	this cut is installed there, continue the interrupted one* order;
	do not assume a green-field re-interview unless PREINSTALL or
	snapshots require it.  Master/umbrella projects must keep pqk as a
	separate kernel deliverable next to (not inside) pqf skills.

